#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kbruch; is a small program to practice calculating with fractions and "
"percentages. Five different exercises are offered as well as a learning mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Arithmetic - in this exercise you have to solve a given fraction task. You "
"have to enter the numerator and the denominator. This is the main exercise."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Comparison - in this exercise you have to compare the size of 2 given "
"fractions, using the symbols <guibutton>&gt;</guibutton>, <guibutton>&lt;</"
"guibutton> or <guibutton>=</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Conversion - in this exercise you have to convert a given number into a "
"fraction."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Factorization - in this exercise you have to factorize a given number into "
"its prime factors."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "Percentage - in this exercise you have to calculate percentages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In each different exercise &kbruch; will generate a task and the user has to "
"solve it. The program checks the input and gives a feedback about it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kbruch; counts how many tasks were solved at all and how many tasks were "
"solved correctly. The statistics are shown to the user."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kbruch; is very compact and focuses on the core idea of a task generator. "
"An online help system provides context-sensitive help for the different "
"situations."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &kbruch;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid "Choosing the mode: learning or exercises"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you start &kbruch;, it offers you two modes: <guilabel>Freestyle</"
"guilabel> which is the training mode and <guilabel>Learning</guilabel> where "
"you can understand fractions. Clicking one of the pictures will enter the "
"chosen mode. Here is a screenshot of &kbruch;'s modes:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>&kbruch; mode choices</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>&kbruch; mode choices</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click one of the picture to choose the mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid "Main freestyle screen"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here is a screenshot of &kbruch;'s main freestyle screen:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kbruch; main screen, directly after the freestyle start"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kbruch; main screen"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All exercises take place in this screen. This ensures that &kbruch; is easy "
"to use even for young users! The main screen is separated into 5 parts: "
"<itemizedlist> <listitem><para> the menubar with the 3 menus <guimenu>File</"
"guimenu>, <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> and <guimenu>Help</guimenu> </para></"
"listitem> <listitem><para> the toolbar, where you can switch between the "
"different exercises </para></listitem> <listitem><para> the "
"<guilabel>Options</guilabel> on the left, where you can define the "
"difficulty and various settings for the tasks </para></listitem> "
"<listitem><para> the task part, where you have to enter the result of the "
"given task </para></listitem> <listitem><para> the statistical part, where "
"you can see how many tasks have been solved correctly or attempted </para></"
"listitem> </itemizedlist> At any time, you can go back to Modes using the "
"<guiicon>Back</guiicon> icon in the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can hide the <guilabel>Options</guilabel> section by dragging it to the "
"left."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First you have to choose an exercise in the toolbar. Default is Arithmetic. "
"The task part will change according to the chosen task. Some settings in the "
"<guilabel>Options</guilabel> section will be enabled, depending on the task "
"you have chosen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You will find an icon to generate a new task in the toolbar as well. This "
"action is also available in the menu <menuchoice><guimenu>File</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>New</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. This action is always "
"enabled. If you have not solved the currently given task, a new task is "
"generated and the given task is counted as not correctly solved."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you terminate &kbruch; the currently chosen exercise will be saved and "
"restored on next startup."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid "Statistical Part"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>&kbruch; statistics</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>&kbruch; statistics</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid "In this part of the main screen you can see:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:225
#, no-c-format
msgid "on the left, how many tasks have been solved"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:228
#, no-c-format
msgid "on the right, in green, how many tasks have been solved correctly"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid "on the right, in red, how many tasks have been solved incorrectly"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:234
#, no-c-format
msgid "on the right, in orange, how many tasks have been skipped"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:239
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can reset the statistics by clicking on the <guimenu>New</guimenu> "
"button in the toolbar or choosing <menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>New</guimenuitem></menuchoice> in the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:244
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The statistics will be saved when &kbruch; is closed and restored on next "
"startup."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:251
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring &kbruch; appearance"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:252
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this dialog you can adjust some general settings for the task display. To "
"open this dialog use <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure &kbruch;</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:260
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>&kbruch; settings dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:266
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>&kbruch; settings dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:271
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are two tabs to adjust the setting:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:278
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Colors</guilabel>: Choose the colors for the different parts of a "
"mathematical expression: numbers, operational sign, fraction bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:282
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Fonts</guilabel>: Choose a font for displaying the task."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:287
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The settings will be saved on &kbruch;'s termination and restored on the "
"next startup."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:294
#, no-c-format
msgid "Main learning screen"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:296
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>&kbruch; learning mode</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:302
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>&kbruch; learning mode</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:306
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking the <guibutton>Hint</guibutton> button toggles the display of the "
"help on the right which explains you how the rings work."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:313
#, no-c-format
msgid "Exercises"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:316
#, no-c-format
msgid "Exercise Fraction Task"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:318
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this exercise you have to solve a given task. Therefore you have to enter "
"the numerator and the denominator. The difficulty of the generated task can "
"be adjusted by using some options on the left."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:324
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Operations"
msgid "Options"
msgstr "Operacions"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:325
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are 3 parameters which influence the difficulty of the generated tasks:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:331
#, no-c-format
msgid "Terms"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:332
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The number of terms (separate fractions) given in each task. From 2 to 5, "
"inclusive."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:337
#, no-c-format
msgid "Max. main denominator"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:338
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The highest number &kbruch; will use as the main denominator in the tasks it "
"sets. From a minimum of 10 to a maximum of 50."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:343
#, no-c-format
msgid "Operations"
msgstr "Operacions"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:344
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Operations which should be used in the task: <guilabel>Addition</guilabel>, "
"<guilabel>Subtraction</guilabel>, <guilabel>Multiplication</guilabel> or "
"<guilabel>Division</guilabel>. Check all operations you want to use."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:351
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After you have changed the parameters you have to click on the <guimenu>New</"
"guimenu> button in the toolbar to generate a task which uses the new "
"parameters. You can also call this action from the menubar with "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Task</guimenu><guimenuitem>New</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:364
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have not solved the current task and call the <guimenu>New</guimenu> "
"action, the task will be counted as not solved correctly. To prevent this "
"you have to change the parameters after you solved the task but before "
"generating a new one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:370
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The chosen parameters will be saved on &kbruch;'s termination and restored "
"on next startup."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:377
#, no-c-format
msgid "Solving Tasks"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:378
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After you have solved a given task, you need to enter the result into the "
"two input boxes. In the upper box you enter the numerator and in the lower "
"box the denominator."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:383
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the result is negative, you can enter a minus sign in front of the "
"numerator or denominator. If the result is 0, just type a 0 in the numerator "
"input field. If the result has a denominator of 1, you can leave the lower "
"box empty."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:388
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After you have entered the result you should click the <guibutton>Check</"
"guibutton> button below the input boxes. &kbruch; will check your input and "
"present the correct result on the right below the <guilabel>Incorrect!</"
"guilabel> string:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:394
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Checked Task</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:400
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Checked Task</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:404
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This task was solved incorrectly. The correct value is shown in 2 different "
"forms: normal (reduced) and mixed number."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:409
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you checked the <guibutton>Reduced form</guibutton> in the Options in the "
"Answers section then you always have to enter the result reduced. &kbruch; "
"will show you a short message like the one in the screenshot below, if you "
"enter the correct result unreduced. The answer will then be counted as "
"incorrect."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:417
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Unreduced Result</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:423
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Unreduced Result</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:428
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To continue with the next task, click on the <guimenu>New</guimenu> button. "
"If you want to change the parameters for the next task please do this before "
"clicking on the <guimenu>New</guimenu> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:437
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Exercise Comparison</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:439
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this exercise you have to compare 2 given fractions. You have to choose "
"the bigger fraction of both by selecting the correct comparison sign."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:444
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Exercise Comparison</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:450
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Exercise Comparison</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:455
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First choose the correct comparison sign. To toggle the comparison sign, you "
"have to click on the button showing the comparison sign. After you have "
"chosen the comparison sign, the result will show on the right. A green "
"square with <guilabel>Correct</guilabel> will tell you that your answer was "
"correct while a red square with <guilabel>Incorrect</guilabel> will indicate "
"that your answer was wrong. You will get to the next task by clicking the "
"<guimenu>Next</guimenu> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:465
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Exercise Conversion</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:467
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this exercise you have to convert a given number into a fraction. You "
"have to enter numerator and denominator."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:472
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Exercise Conversion</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:478
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Exercise Conversion</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:483
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the left side of the equal sign in the screenshot above you can see a "
"recurring decimal. This means, that the fraction shown as a decimal has a "
"repeating part. The repeating part is marked with the small bar above the "
"numbers. Those numbers repeat ad infinitum."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:489
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After you have entered the numerator and denominator click on the "
"<guimenu>Check Task</guimenu> button. &kbruch; will check your input and "
"present the correct result. After this step you will get to the next task by "
"clicking on the <guimenu>New</guimenu> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:496
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Do not forget to enter the result reduced. Unreduced results will be counted "
"as solved not correctly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:504
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Exercise Factorization</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:506
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this exercise you have to factorize a given number into its prime "
"factors. You have to enter all prime factors of the number."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:511
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Exercise Factorization</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:517
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Exercise Factorization</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:522
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can enter a factor by clicking on the prime factor buttons. The "
"<quote>*</quote> sign is automatically inserted, when you click the next "
"prime factor button. You can remove the last entered prime factor by "
"clicking on the <guimenu>Remove Last Factor</guimenu> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:527
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After you have entered all prime factors click on the <guimenu>Check Task</"
"guimenu> button. &kbruch; will check your input and present the correct "
"result. After this step you will get to the next task by clicking on the "
"<guimenu>New</guimenu> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:534
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the screenshot at the top of this page you can see a <quote>*</quote> "
"between the prime factors. This is the multiplication sign. The product of "
"all prime factors must be the number you try to factorize."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:540
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You have to enter all prime factors even when a prime factor repeats several "
"times. Example: As prime factors of number 18 you have to enter 2, 3 and 3."
msgstr ""

